For /14, /340 and /362, full diffs between campaigns differ only in the
generator-options comment and trailing bitfield-statistics comment. Their
executable text is identical, not merely assumed identical from the seed.

Source-bound reasons:
* /14 func_1:93-215. The preceding func_12 only initializes locals and returns
  its argument. g_25/g_973 still address g_26[3][0], while l_1025 addresses
  distinct g_26[0][2] (0x53494abc). The former receives signed-halfword
  0x4abc % 0xbfe4 = 2720; the latter is unchanged. The seven-iteration byte
  loop terminates at 32, then the nonzero const g_449 jumps back before its
  outer update. The alternate branch and its calls cannot be reached.
* /340 func_1:75-115, func_6:142-150. func_6 skips its initialized -9 == 16
  loop, changes only g_10/g_227 and returns the unchanged g_375. The other
  callee returns its argument. The u8 g_433 loop breaks on its first visit.
  g_347 points to a halfword equal to 1; (1 == ((-7) || -9)) ^ -9 is -10,
  less than g_37[2][6] (0x5bb0). The false arm tests unchanged nonzero g_315
  and jumps back. No reachable write changes that comparison or guard.
* /362 func_38:259-345. Its initial caller passes p_40=-1 and p_41=g_26[3]=0;
  preceding func_18 changes g_29, not g_26. p_41 is a value, so writing -10
  through g_35 in the callee does not change it. g_51=9 and l_49=0 reset;
  u16 g_16=-12 skips ==42 and all calls in that body. The false p_41 arm
  increments an unrelated u8 and jumps back before either induction update.
* base/161 func_13:170-214. The first p_15=0 iteration sets g_23=0 and skips
  >=12, including the only g_322 decrement. g_322 is initially 5 and has no
  other preceding write; its true branch restarts p_15 at zero. The continued
  p_15!=0 path and later calls do not precede that restart.
* base/204 func_1:122-152. Array initialization resets g_3/g_4, then g_3=-12.
  Equal array elements subtract to zero. g_4's finite 0..-20 loop skips its
  inner g_12=0/==60 loop. Unchanged g_3 is nonzero and restarts initialization
  before its own increment; there is no call or write through the pointer array.
* bitfields/26 func_1:100-165. g_2=25 skips <=-21, including every call and
  every change to g_186 or g_33. Equal operands subtract to zero and the
  subsequent u16 add writes g_2=1. Nonzero g_186=-4 selects the true branch;
  g_33.f0=0xd534 restarts before g_72's first update. These are ordinary
  union halfword accesses, not an assumption about bitfield arithmetic.
* bitfields/104 func_42:441-455. g_33 is u8: -9 becomes 247 and skips <=33,
  including both calls and all writes in the body. The remaining pointer
  store cannot address g_117 (its address never occurs in this program).
  g_117 starts nonzero; the only other assignments initialize it to 1 or
  increment it to at most 7. Its backward branch therefore stays true.

